From ee3210f414cc7319bd8faa488850b4955150d8d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 14:53:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/40] RenderEngine: import NV12 dmabufs directly via
 samplerExternalOES
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the custom YUV→RGB shader converter (added in 0009) with direct
multi-plane EGLImage import. Mesa Panfrost (and most modern drivers) handle
YUV→RGB at sample time inside samplerExternalOES based on the EGL color
space hint, so the intermediate FBO/shader/texture is unnecessary.

The shader converter had two latent bugs that broke compositing after any
HW-decoded video frame:

1. glDisableVertexAttribArray(posLoc) disabled attrib 0 (Program::position),
   which Program::Program() enables exactly once at construction. Subsequent
   layer draws read constant (0,0,0,1) for position, collapsing every
   triangle to the origin — no GL error, no visible output.

2. The persistent mNv12OutputTex/mNv12OutputEGLImage was aliased to the
   layer's texName via glEGLImageTargetTexture2DOES. After the layer was
   destroyed and the texName recycled by another layer, Mali's driver kept
   the previous EGLImage association, so the new layer sampled the last
   decoded video frame instead of its own buffer.

The new path is ~50 lines, has no persistent GL state, and creates a fresh
single-plane-described EGLImage per frame (destroyed immediately after the
texture references it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ifb3fe09627d8ccab919d0f1d74a2d40147ff17ce
